    "updated_at": "2025-11-14T21:25:49Z",
    "body": "While not a new pseudo-state, I think the situation described by @bkardell could be improved at least with a pattern I've been calling self-destructing CSS. So instead of this:\n\n```\n:not(:defined) { visibility: hidden; }\n```\n\nTry this:\n\n```\n@keyframes hideBriefly {\n  0%, 100% { visibility: hidden; } \n}\n:not(:defined) { animation: hideBriefly 2s; }\n ```\n\nIn this post about it, I use opacity and I'm unsure which is preferable here. https://scottjehl.com/posts/this-css-will-self-destruct/",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
